of Human Evolution</article-title><source>PNAS</source><year>2007</year><volume>104</volume><fpage>17614</fpage><lpage>17619</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17978179</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.0708280104</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>MG</given-names></name><name><surname>Parfill</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Weiss</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Skorecki</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Roux</surname><given-names>Ml</given-names></name><name><surname>Bradman</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldstein</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Y Chromosomes Traveling Sough: The Cohen Modal Haplotype and the Origins of the Lemba &#x02013; the "Black Jews of Southern Africa"</article-title><source>Am J Hum Genet</source><year>2000</year><volume>66</volume><fpage>674</fpage><lpage>686</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10677325</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/302749</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beckman</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Sikstrom</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Midelsaar</surname><given-names>AV</given-names></name><name><surname>Krumina</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ambrasiene</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Kucinskas</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Beckman</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tranferrin Varients as Markers of Migrations and Admixtures between Populations in the Baltic Sea Region</article-title><source>Human Heredity</source><year>1998</year><volume>48</volume><fpage>185</fpage><lpage>191</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9694249</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1159/000022800</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Falush</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Wirth</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Linz</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Pritchard</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name><name><surname>Stephens</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kidd</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Blaser</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Graham</surname><given-names>DY</given-names></name><name><surname>Vacher</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Perez-Perez</surname><given-names>GI</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Traces of human migrations in <italic>Helicobacter pylori </italic>populations</article-title><source>Science</source><year>2003</year><volume>299</volume><fpage>1582</fpage><lpage>1585</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12624269</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1126/science.1080857</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McGhee</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Contact between Native Americans and the Medieval Norse: A Review of the Evidence</article-title><source>American Antiquity</source><year>1984</year><volume>49</volume><fpage>4</fpage><lpage>26</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/280509</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Klar</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Linguistic Evidence for a Prehistoric Polynesia-Southern California Contact Event</article-title><source>Anthropological LInguistics</source><year>2005</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>369</fpage><lpage>400</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Allen</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>More on the Free Black Population of the Southern Appalachian Mountains: Speculations on the North African Connection</article-title><source>Journal of Black Studies</source><year>1995</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>651</fpage><lpage>671</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1177/002193479502500601</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Epstein</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Buchanan</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name><name><surname>Buttrey</surname><given-names>TV</given-names></name><name><surname>Carter</surname><given-names>GF</given-names></name><name><surname>Cook;</surname><given-names>WL</given-names></name><name><surname>Covey</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Jett</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Mundkur</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Paulsen</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Pre-Columbian Old World Coins in America: An Examination of the Evidence</article-title><source>Current Anthropology</source><year>1980</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>20</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/202398</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Quaife</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The My